{
  "id": "Compound::DB00396 - Gene::1557",
  "verbalization": "Progesterone is implicated in the regulation of Cyp2c19 through a series of molecular interactions that involve the enzyme Cyp2a6 and its related activities. The evidence suggests that Progesterone binds to Cyp2a6, which then participates in the oxidation of arachidonic acid, a process that is also carried out by Cyp2c19. This indicates a potential functional overlap between these two enzymes, where Progesterone may influence the activity of Cyp2c19 through the modulation of Cyp2a6. The presence of a lowest common ancestor (LCA) between Progesterone and Felbamate, which binds to Cyp2c19, further supports a mechanistic link between Progesterone and Cyp2c19, suggesting that Progesterone may indirectly affect Cyp2c19 through the action of Felbamate. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible role for Progesterone in modulating Cyp2c19 activity, though the exact nature of this relationship remains to be fully elucidated.",
